A 2019 meta-analysis in the Journal of the American Heart Association found plant-based diets reduce cardiovascular disease risk by 32% compared to omnivorous diets.
Type 2 diabetes incidence is 23% lower in vegetarians and 38% lower in vegans compared to meat eaters, according to a 2009 study of 60,000 people in the EPIC-Oxford cohort.
The WHO's International Agency for Research on Cancer classifies processed meat as a Group 1 carcinogen (causes colorectal cancer) — substituting plant protein reduces this exposure.
